I’ve sorted out 11 structural validation rules for map nodes in Workflow.parse:
1. Source must be either depends_on or a task node;
2. Paths can’t be empty, use dot-separated format, and traversal only targets dicts;
3. Template IDs must be unique across all node and template IDs;
4. Map nodes can’t be placed in loop bodies, and loops can’t depend on map nodes;
5. Task nodes can safely depend on map nodes;
6. Map nodes can depend on loops;
7. Duplicate template IDs are prohibited;
8. The current loop validation logic needs to be extended to cover map nodes;
9. Map nodes can be referenced as dependencies for other nodes;
10. Only task nodes carry run_if attributes;
11. Template IDs can’t conflict with map IDs.

I’ve confirmed that source-in-depends_on logic is map-specific, and will add a dedicated map validation check after the acyclic and loop validation steps. I’ll also add a Workflow property to conveniently retrieve all map node IDs, and the existing parse logic remains unchanged.

